WEBVTT

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.400
Please.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.530
I can only rely on your skills.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.900
Please accept.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.780
I'll do it.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.370
Thank you.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.370
Now I can widen my prospects.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.290
Well, I'll leave it in your hands.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.540
I am not one to entrust my dominant arm to others.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.090
So I don't shake hands.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.930
S-Sorry. I'll obey all your rules.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.180
Don't do more than necessary until the job is complete.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.690
Uh, right... I'll just sit back and be quiet.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.030
Who the hell does he think he is?

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:58.830
Damn gook.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.900
Hurry and call the police!

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.030
No good, these two are already dead!

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.780
H-Hey! This guy's alive!

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.450
Get an ambulance!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.920
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.050
wondering what I should do right now.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:03.510
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.060
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.690
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.110
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.580
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.870
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.170
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.260
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:45.350
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.940
depend on me for your repairs.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.320
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:55.530 --> 00:03:01.530
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.830
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:11.870
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:24.720
Arms of an Angel, Arms of The Devil

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.440
What was that?

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.940
Why can't I perform the operation?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.240
But the glass shards from the car lacerated his right arm.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.370
We would need to get Dr. Cutter for wounds as serious as those.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.620
He's off duty!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.040
Geez, it's just "Cutter! Cutter!" with you people!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.710
Poor man.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:02.180
If we let that surgeon operate on him, he'd only be capable of restoring motion to his wrists.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.220
You mentioned a Dr. Cutter earlier?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.220
That's right, you haven't met him yet.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.850
He's our orthopedic surgeon.
I swear he has the arms of an angel!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.860
Arms of an angel?

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:20.990
Dr. Cutter is the only one who can completely heal this patient's arm.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.310
This is all so resplendent, Mr. Wassant.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.320
Oh, it's all because of you kind people.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.360
Well you are the biggest philanthropist in North America.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.320
And you're throwing this benefit to help orphans.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.830
I'm just trying to raise funds for my orphanage.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.210
Even at that, it's nothing to sneeze at.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.210
Not only do you raise orphans, but you turn them into successful members of society.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.550
Thank you.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.880
Your support means...

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.720
I almost forgot.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.890
Let me step back and show you all
something of actual interest tonight.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:33.850
Yang!

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:34.980
Yang!

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.400
Allow me to introduce him.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.860
He was one of the orphans I raised.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:44.740
Yang.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.240
Show them what you can do.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.750
From the left, Beethoven's Ninth Symphony...

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.260
...Wagner's <i>Die Walküre</i>

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.760
...and Schubert's <i>Erlkönig.</i>

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.760
What about the fourth one?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.720
That wasn't very fair of you adding in a pop music CD.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.890
Shirley Bassey's "Goldfinger."

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.560
Brava!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.860
Wonderful!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.190
Dad.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.490
I have work early tomorrow, so I have to leave now.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.860
Is that so? In that case, you can take the car.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.030
Thank you.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.330
If you'll excuse me, I have to get going.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:42.250
Mr. Wassant, who is he? Does he have superpowers? Or is he a magician?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:48.220
No, all he did was read the slight unevenness made by the printed text on the CDs.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.380
He actually did that?

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.890
He's a top-flight surgeon.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.640
He's able to locate small nerves and muscles

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.690
and operate on them flawlessly while closing his eyes and relying on the acute sensitivity of his fingers.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.280
His name is Yang Lee Cutter.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.990
That man truly has the arms of an angel.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.970
You are our pride and joy.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.680
Now cut that out, Fred.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:35.970
The fact that you're always right
there for our dad puts me at ease.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.350
Actually, one of Dad's subordinates has just been killed.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.310
What?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.480
Although Dad came and saved us immigrant kids

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.650
it seems that it was done by those who didn't consider that.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.860
Dad was involved in some mischievous stuff back when he was younger.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.860
Yeah.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.870
The work he's doing now is his way for atoning for those sins.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:08.840
What do you want?

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:14.300
Sorry I couldn't come to the party, Samuel Beaulieu Wassant.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.680
I didn't bother inviting you.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.310
There's still a very important package I need to get.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.980
I'm afraid you're not going to be getting it.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.190
What?

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.230
I'm sure people will be in complete shock

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:38.870
if they find out that the candidate for governor, Albert Stantz, was the former leader of a ruthless street gang, the Illinois Angels...

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.580
...who robbed, raped and even murdered all in the name of "anarchism."

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.750
And you were the boss, Stantz.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.000
The same goes for you.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.760
That's right.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:57.090
I may be able to erase my gang
tattoo, but I cannot erase my past.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.850
Hmph, fine then.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.520
I only called to give you a report.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.020
A report?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.520
I called a hit man over to Chicago. A sniper at the top of his game.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:11.570
If you hand over the photo, I'll rethink my decision.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.860
You should rethink everything.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:19.530
Pull out of the governor's race, or else I'll publicize the photo.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:22.040
That way I'll take the winds out of your sails.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.040
Do that, and you'll be going down.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.540
If I take you down too, then all the better.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.090
That's a shame. And we go back such a long way too.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.220
Well, be sure to think this through.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:38.050
Is this really something worth losing your life over?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.150
A sniper at the top of his game...

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.280
No alcohol for me, I'm driving remember?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.070
You can just leave it here.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.500
Dr. Cutter?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.790
You lowlife!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:15.510
Hey-

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.050
Fred!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.010
He's only stunned.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.510
W-Who are you?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:22.640
My arm.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.970
Take a look at my arm.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.100
If that's the case, get to the hospital!

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.600
It's my charts.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.730
I heard about how good you are.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.990
So I want you to operate on my arm.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.990
This <i>is</i>  a serious injury.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.280
I will pay you the appropriate compensation. Will you accept?

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.240
I can't.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:49.370
I can't immediately operate on a patient with lacerations as severe as yours.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:54.750
Because of the severe paralysis, we won't be
able to finely locate and confirm all your injuries.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.970
We will need to apply some stop-gap treatment, then keep you under observation for three to six weeks.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.640
Then only after a thorough examination do we conduct a surgery.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.220
There's no time!

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.100
Do it now.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:14.320
I'll use my fingertips to determine what's been damaged in the affected area.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.730
It's going to take a lot of time.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.110
Overlooking anything will be out of the question.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.110
You're still willing to go through with it?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.620
Do it.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.870
Okay. I'll do what I can.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.540
Before that, I need to see both of your arms.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:41.340
I need to confirm with my own hand if
your dexterity does live up to its fame.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.900
<i>What's this sensation I'm getting?</i>

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.520
<i>Who is this man?</i>

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.330
Are you sure you don't want any anesthesia?

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.090
No need.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.330
You must have heard of him at least once.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.420
Golgo 13.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.590
They say he has the arms of the Devil.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:48.340
I'm glad you know. Once I give the
word, Golgo 13 will not pull the trigger.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.600
So what say you?

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.260
Fred.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:52.970
Yes?

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.850
Please show these two out.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.190
Are you aware of what you just said?

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.520
Of course.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.190
You fool! You've just hastened your own death!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.080
That wasn't a good idea.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.250
What wasn't?

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.210
Name dropping Golgo 13.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.790
You're just bluffing about how you can call it off, right?

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.250
If Golgo himself gets word of that...

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.760
He'll rub me out?

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:31.510
Golgo considers clients who go against his rules as equivalent to traitors.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.970
How is he going to hear about that?

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:39.020
In any case, we get the photo once Wassant is killed.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.900
I will make the arrangements.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.950
Okay, make a fist.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.950
Slowly...

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:55.830
Open.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:02.170
Okay, it's been three weeks since the surgery yet you made an astounding recovery.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:10.050
Since things seem fine, we can now do
a thorough examination at the hospital.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.300
No, you can do that using just your eyes and fingers.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:20.140
What's your connection to Samuel Beaulieu Wassant?

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:20.770
Huh?

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.060
You took that photo with Mr. Wassant, didn't you?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.990
Yeah. I owe him everything.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.320
He's like a father to me.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.820
I'm a Chinese immigrant.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:39.960
My parents died while I was young, and I scraped by alone using my natural dexterity to pick pockets.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.710
That's when I met Dad.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.420
He took me in and raised me.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:53.140
The fact that he recognized my gift and helped to finance
my college education is the reason you see me here today.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.390
If it wasn't for Dad, I'd now be...

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:01.350
It's also thanks to Dad that your arm has miraculously healed.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:07.980
Excuse me.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.570
Hello?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:11.990
Oh, Fred.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.700
How's the arm? Who's arm?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.910
Uh, right...

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.790
Actually, there's still some loose ends...

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.210
What did you say?

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.130
That man is after our father's life.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.000
He's called Golgo 13.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.130
He a world famous sniper who's has no peer.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:32.760
A sniper?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:37.550
When he comes for another examination
you're going to be performing another surgery.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:43.140
If you sever a nerve during that time, you'll render his right arm useless.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.400
As a doctor I can't do that.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.900
Do you want him to kill our dad?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.030
Yes?

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.620
It's me... Duke Togo.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.660
Oh, it's you!

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.620
Send the M-16s over to Chicago.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:10.880
What? Why spring <i>that</i>  on me?

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:20.470
I'm never able to follow his requests.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.230
What the hell is that Golgo 13 doing?!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.060
There's only five days left till the election!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:34.740
I can't even sleep soundly what with me worrying
about when Wassant is going to release that photo!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.070
What if he did actually find out?

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:38.740
Huh?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.490
The fact that you used Golgo's name to threaten Wassant.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.910
I know.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:47.170
As long as you keep quiet, he's not going to find out!

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.630
You're right, but...

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.200
Please, Dad, get away from Chicago!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.870
I'm begging you with my life!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:26.660
Yang.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.210
I've made my peace with the fact that Golgo is going to kill me.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:35.050
The time has come for me to pay the debts for the life I lived.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.550
Dad...

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.430
The photographic evidence is in a bank safety deposit box.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:49.940
When I die, I want you to release that photo.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.530
Looks like I've lost.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.520
Who the hell would leave their gun at the crime scene?

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:32.940
Hmm?

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.030
Hey, lemme see that gun!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.280
I knew it.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:49.040
This gun was modded to be used by a left-hander.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.040
Left-hand?

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.510
It appears I've been over-thinking things.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.970
I salute you, Golgo 13.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.810
You are certainly worth your high asking price.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:11.520
All we have left is to retrieve that photo.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.730
That is the case.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.030
Yes?

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.320
Golgo!

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.790
You <i>will</i>  play by the rules... Mr. Stantz.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.290
What the heck did Golgo tell you?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.510
He knew about... how I...

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:44.010
...how I broke his rules.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:56.150
Hey!

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:56.730
What?

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:57.730
He's been shot!

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.360
H-He's been shot!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:20:59.940
How did it happened?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:07.450
We believe that the shootings of Messrs. Wassants and Stantz were the works of the same criminal.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:13.460
The offender also purposely left a left-handed and a right-handed rifle at the crime scenes.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.710
Do you know the meaning behind that? Any idea at all?

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.810
Dad, Stantz is dead.

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:37.900
I don't know the reason why, but it appears that Golgo was behind it.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.690
We don't need this any longer.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:47.700
He probably used his left arm to carry out his job as an obligation to me.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:52.240
You think that guy even has a sense of duty or obligation?

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:55.540
He's just a dirty rat prick who dances to the tune of money!

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:05.170
Where are you heading?

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.720
The airport.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:11.850
Take me there.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:47.130
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:50.180
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:52.350
without moving a muscle.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:55.520
I wonder when that was?

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:57.230
I'm sure

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:00.400
you agonized over how

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:05.650
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.900
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.030
When

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:13.450
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.700
you never change.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:17.950
Since you're here for me

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:22.250
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.500
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:29.840
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:36.720
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:39.890
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:43.230
